            <ArticleTitle>Fatal granulomatous disease of childhood: presenting as acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fatal granulomatous disease of childhood is a rare disorder of phagocytic function. We report a 6-year-old boy who presented with acute abdomen. The diagnosis was established by mesenteric lymph node biopsy obtained at laparotomy. The boy succumbed within hours of surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
